{
  "id": "indirect-portal",
  "title": "A red destination lights the white floor through its acquired portal image",
  "binding": "A fixed camera looks at a white floor beside a window session onto a red emissive destination. Root analytic lights, material emission, sky and fill are zero. The enabled Screens category must appear in the same fenced floor pick and in the floor capture. The opposite changes only authored render.indirect.sources.screens to zero, while the destination still renders red. The root uses Medium and the existing current-source fence. The pointer station and conservative red image bounds require actual World confirmation; unsupported or absent incoming data fails rather than borrowing another response. This image canary does not substitute for finite mutual closure, whole-epoch acquired pixel immutability, cold-history equivalence, external-source taint, nested budget or warmed crossing laws.",
  "bootShape": "offscreen",
  "backends": [
    "vulkan",
    "directx"
  ],
  "requirements": [
    "gpu"
  ],
  "timeoutSeconds": 60,
  "fixtures": [
    "red-room.puck",
    "README.md"
  ],
